@startuml

title BEAST - Input/current generator architecture

left to right direction
hide empty members
hide circle

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

package "beast-py: beast.generators" {
    abstract class Generator {
        - t_start : float
        - t_stop : float
        - delta_t : float
        - Ng : int
        + duration : float
        + n_samples : int
        {abstract} + generate_all(t_start, t_stop, delta_t)
        {abstract} + generate_t(t)
        + time_vector(n_samples, delta_t, t_start)
        + t_all : Vector
    }

    class Generator_ConstantValue {
        + generate() : (Vector, Vector)
    }

    class Generator_Pulse {
        + n_high_samples : int
        + n_low_samples : int
        + generate() : (Vector, Vector)
    }

    Generator <|-- Generator_ConstantValue
    Generator <|-- Generator_Pulse
}

package "beast-mat: beast.CurrentGenerators" {
    class CurrentPWL <<function>>
    class CurrentPulse <<function>>
    class CurrentPulsed01 <<function>>
}

Generator_Pulse .. CurrentPulse : related pulse concept

note bottom
  The generator subsystems share a purpose but not a portable class contract.
  Python uses stateful classes; MATLAB exposes independent functions.
  CurrentPWL and CurrentPulsed01 have no direct Python counterparts;
  Generator_ConstantValue has no direct MATLAB counterpart.
end note

@enduml
